-- ===========================================================================
-- Income Tax Ordinance s 47(d) and the Income Tax (Deduction of Payments for Benefits or Pension) Regulations, 5740-1980. Row IL-27.
-- Source: ITO lines 1788-1789; the Regulations, regulations/income-tax-deduction-of-payments-for-benefits-or-pension-regulations-5740-1980.he.wiki.txt
-- lines 14-25.
--
-- s 47(d) lets the Minister, with the Finance Committee's approval, set deductions at rates higher than those of s 47(b) for a class of people. The
-- Regulations of 5740-1980 do so for an individual who has completed 50 years at the start of the tax year (regulation 2):
--   (a)(1) 10.5% of the qualifying income to which s 47(b)(1) applies, not above "the ceiling of the deduction";
--   (a)(2) one who paid for pension only, and paid more than the amount allowed under (1) plus 5% of that qualifying income, may deduct the excess
--          up to a further 6% of that income, the total not above the ceiling;
--   (b)    7.5% of the qualifying income to which s 47(b)(2) applies, not above the ceiling.
-- Regulation 1: "the ceiling of the deduction" is the product of "the rates fixed as a deduction in s 47(b)(1) or (b)(2) of the Ordinance, as the case
-- may be" and "the ceiling of the qualifying income as meant in s 47(a)(1)". Regulation 3: from the 1979 tax year (inert: this row answers tax years
-- from 2024).
--
-- WHAT IS READ FROM THE TEXT.
-- * Age: "שמלאו לו בתחילת שנת המס 50 שנה" is read as 50 completed years on the first day of the tax year (a birthday on 1 January counts) (NOTES.md A7).
-- * The Regulations concern s 47(b); a beneficiary member is under (b1), which they do not touch, so he is deducted under IL-08's (b1).
-- * "the qualifying income to which s 47(b)(1) applies" is IL-08's non-work part of the qualifying income; "to which s 47(b)(2) applies", its work part
--   less insured income, as in IL-08 (its fork F6). The ceiling "as the case may be": the s 47(a)(1) paragraph (2) amount for (b)(1), paragraph (1)
--   amount for (b)(2) (NOTES.md A6).
-- * The deduction is of "the sums paid" ("אם שילם"): the lesser of them and the limits, as in s 47(b). "The sum he paid" in (a)(2) is the sums
--   paid under s 47(b) in total.
-- * The facts the Regulations add are the date of birth and whether he paid for a pension only ("בעד קיצבה בלבד"), an input.
-- * The order of the deduction and the s 45A credit is IL-08's fork F35, with IL-08's reading type; the enlarged deduction takes the place of the deduction there.
--
-- TWO FORKS, each RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08 (SHRUG) as one named switch, default declined where the readings give different deductions, each reading kept
-- by name and tested; and a third considered and found no fork.
-- F12  the ceiling of regulation 1. "The rates fixed as a deduction in s 47(b)(1)": the first rate of the paragraph (7%), or every rate of it (7% and the
--      further 4%, so 11%). Paragraph (2) has one rate (5%). The two give different ceilings for (b)(1) when the enlarged deduction passes 7% of the ceiling.
-- F13  (considered, no switch) regulation 2(b): "7.5% of the qualifying income to which s 47(b)(2) applies". s 47(b)(2) is the lower of two amounts at 5%: either the
--      7.5% replaces the 5% in both, or it is 7.5% of the first limb's income alone. On IL-08's definitions (insured income taken into the qualifying work income
--      first, its fork F6) the second limb's income is never the lower: min(work, 2.5 x c) - insured >= min(work, c) - insured. The two readings never differ, so
--      there is no switch, and the 7.5% is applied to both limbs as written. Were F6 read the other way, F13 would bite.
-- F14  regulation 2: "the rate of deduction under s 47(b) ... shall be". Either the rate it gives replaces the rate of s 47(b), or the individual has the
--      higher of the two (the title is "enlarged deduction"). They differ where the enlarged deduction is the lesser, which happens for one who paid more
--      than 12% and not for a pension only.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Section 47(d) — the Regulations of 5740-1980`

§§ `Quotations`

-- src:1788 | (ד) שר האוצר, באישור ועדת הכספים של הכנסת, רשאי לקבוע ניכויים בשיעורים גבוהים מהאמורים בסעיף קטן (ב) לסוג מסויים של בני־אדם ובתנאים ובסייגים שיקבע.
-- src:1789 | [note: פורסמו תקנות מס הכנסה (ניכוי תשלומים בעד תגמולים או קיצבה), תש״ם–1980.]
-- ext:[reg47:16] | ”תקרת הניכוי“ – הסכום שמתקבל ממכפלת השיעורים הקבועים כניכוי בסעיפים 47(ב)(1) או 47(ב)(2) לפקודה, הכל לפי הענין, בתקרת ההכנסה המזכה כמשמעותה בסעיף 47(א)(1).
-- ext:[reg47:19] | שעור הניכוי לפי סעיף 47(ב) לפקודה בשל תשלומים בעד תגמולים או קיצבה שזכאי לו יחיד שמלאו לו בתחילת שנת המס 50 שנה, יהיה –
-- ext:[reg47:20] | (א)(1) 10.5% מהכנסתו המזכה, שחל עליה סעיף 47(ב)(1) לפקודה ובלבד שסכום הניכוי לא יעלה על תקרת הניכוי;
-- ext:[reg47:21] | (2) מי ששילם בעד קיצבה בלבד והסכום ששילם עולה על הסכום המותר בניכוי על פי פסקה (1), בתוספת 5% מהכנסתו המזכה, יותר לו, בשל החלק העודף, ניכוי נוסף עד ל־6% מאותה הכנסה, ובלבד שהסכום הכולל של הניכוי לא יעלה על תיקרת הניכוי;
-- ext:[reg47:22] | (ב) 7.5% מהכנסתו המזכה שחל עליה סעיף 47(ב)(2) לפקודה ובלבד שסכום הניכוי לא יעלה על תיקרת הניכוי.
-- ext:[reg47:25] | תחילתן של תקנות אלה משנת המס 1979.

§§ `Refusals`

@ref the Regulations of 5740-1980, regulation 1; fork F12
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`regulation 1 defines the ceiling of the deduction by the rates fixed in section 47(b)(1) or (2) and does not say whether that is the first rate or every rate of the paragraph, and here the readings differ` MEANS
    REFUSE "regulation 1 defines the ceiling of the deduction by the rates fixed in section 47(b)(1) or (2) and does not say whether that is the first rate or every rate of the paragraph, and here the readings differ"

@ref the Regulations of 5740-1980, regulation 2; fork F14
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Regulations of 5740-1980 do not say whether the rate they give replaces the rate of section 47(b) or leaves the individual the higher of the two, and here the readings differ` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Regulations of 5740-1980 do not say whether the rate they give replaces the rate of section 47(b) or leaves the individual the higher of the two, and here the readings differ"

@ref the Regulations of 5740-1980; forks F12, F14; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `The readings of the Regulations of 5740-1980`
`the Regulations of 5740-1980 — the readings row IL-27 takes` MEANS
    `The readings of the Regulations of 5740-1980` OF `declined where the readings differ`, `declined where the readings differ`

§§ `Age and the qualifying income`

@ref the Regulations of 5740-1980, regulation 2, line 19 ("שמלאו לו בתחילת שנת המס 50 שנה")
GIVEN born IS A DATE
      `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`one born on` born `has completed 50 years at the start of tax year` `the year` MEANS
    `the year` MINUS DATE_YEAR born MINUS (IF DATE_MONTH born TIMES 100 PLUS DATE_DAY born GREATER THAN 101 THEN 1 ELSE 0) AT LEAST 50

§§ `Regulation 2 under concrete readings`

-- (a)(1) and (a)(2): the limit on the qualifying income to which s 47(b)(1) applies, the non-work part.
@ref the Regulations of 5740-1980, regulation 1 and regulation 2(a), lines 16, 20, 21; fork F12
GIVEN c IS A `A reading of the ceiling of the deduction in regulation 1`
      i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      g IS AN `An individual's age and kind of payment, for the Regulations of 5740-1980`
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 2(a) — the limit on income to which section 47(b)(1) applies, the ceiling being read as` c `, for` i `and` g `, at` a MEANS
    IF   g's `paid for a pension only`
    THEN min `the ceiling` (`allowed under (1)` PLUS `further`)
    ELSE `allowed under (1)`
    WHERE
        `the income`        MEANS `s 47(a)(1) — the part of the qualifying income that is not work income:` i `,` a
        `the rate`          MEANS CONSIDER c
                                  WHEN `the first rate of the paragraph` THEN 7%
                                  WHEN `every rate of the paragraph` THEN 7% PLUS 4%
                                  WHEN `declined where the readings differ` THEN 7%
        `the ceiling`       MEANS `the rate` TIMES a's `the amount in paragraph (2) of the definition of qualifying income`
        `allowed under (1)` MEANS min (10.5% TIMES `the income`) `the ceiling`
        `paid`              MEANS `s 47(b) — the sums that may be deducted, for` i
        `excess`            MEANS max 0 (`paid` MINUS (`allowed under (1)` PLUS 5% TIMES `the income`))
        `further`           MEANS min `excess` (6% TIMES `the income`)

-- (b): the limit on the qualifying income to which s 47(b)(2) applies, the work part less the insured income (fork F13: no switch).
@ref the Regulations of 5740-1980, regulation 1 and regulation 2(b), lines 16, 22; fork F13 (considered)
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 2(b) — the limit on income to which section 47(b)(2) applies, for` i `, at` a MEANS
    min `the ceiling` (7.5% TIMES min `first limb` `second limb`)
    WHERE
        `the ceiling` MEANS 5% TIMES a's `the amount in paragraph (1) of the definition of qualifying income`
        `first limb`  MEANS max 0 (`s 47(a)(1) — the part of the qualifying income that is work income:` i `,` a MINUS i's `insured income`)
        `second limb` MEANS max 0 (min (i's `taxable income from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A`) (2.5 TIMES a's `the amount in paragraph (1) of the definition of qualifying income`) MINUS i's `insured income`)

-- The enlarged deduction under a concrete reading of the ceiling: the lesser of the sums paid and the two limits.
@ref the Regulations of 5740-1980, regulations 1, 2; fork F12
GIVEN c IS A `A reading of the ceiling of the deduction in regulation 1`
      i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      g IS AN `An individual's age and kind of payment, for the Regulations of 5740-1980`
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 2 — the enlarged deduction, the ceiling being read as` c `, for` i `and` g `, at` a MEANS
    min (`s 47(b) — the sums that may be deducted, for` i)
        (`regulation 2(a) — the limit on income to which section 47(b)(1) applies, the ceiling being read as` c `, for` i `and` g `, at` a
         PLUS `regulation 2(b) — the limit on income to which section 47(b)(2) applies, for` i `, at` a)

-- Regulation 2 against s 47(b) (fork F14), for a concrete reading of the ceiling.
@ref the Regulations of 5740-1980, regulation 2; fork F14
GIVEN c  IS A `A reading of the ceiling of the deduction in regulation 1`
      ag IS A `A reading of regulation 2 against section 47(b)`
      i  IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      g  IS AN `An individual's age and kind of payment, for the Regulations of 5740-1980`
      a  IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 2 — the deduction, the ceiling being read as` c `and the regulation against section 47(b) as` ag `, for` i `and` g `, at` a MEANS
    CONSIDER ag
    WHEN `the regulation replaces the rate of section 47(b)` THEN `enlarged`
    WHEN `the individual has the higher of the two`          THEN max `enlarged` `ordinary`
    WHEN `declined where the readings differ`                THEN `enlarged`
    WHERE
        `enlarged` MEANS `regulation 2 — the enlarged deduction, the ceiling being read as` c `, for` i `and` g `, at` a
        `ordinary` MEANS `s 47(b) — the deduction, for` i `, at` a

§§ `The readings, resolved`

-- A declined reading is resolved by evaluating the concrete readings it stands for: if they agree, that deduction; if not, the reading's refusal.
-- Second level: regulation 2 against s 47(b) (fork F14), the ceiling being concrete.
@ref the Regulations of 5740-1980; fork F14
GIVEN ag IS A `A reading of regulation 2 against section 47(b)`
      c  IS A `A reading of the ceiling of the deduction in regulation 1`
      i  IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      g  IS AN `An individual's age and kind of payment, for the Regulations of 5740-1980`
      a  IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`regulation 2 — resolving the regulation against section 47(b) as` ag `, the ceiling being` c `, for` i `and` g `, at` a MEANS
    CONSIDER ag
    WHEN `declined where the readings differ` THEN
        IF   `regulation 2 — the deduction, the ceiling being read as` c `and the regulation against section 47(b) as` `the regulation replaces the rate of section 47(b)` `, for` i `and` g `, at` a
             EQUALS `regulation 2 — the deduction, the ceiling being read as` c `and the regulation against section 47(b) as` `the individual has the higher of the two` `, for` i `and` g `, at` a
        THEN `regulation 2 — the deduction, the ceiling being read as` c `and the regulation against section 47(b) as` `the regulation replaces the rate of section 47(b)` `, for` i `and` g `, at` a
        ELSE `the Regulations of 5740-1980 do not say whether the rate they give replaces the rate of section 47(b) or leaves the individual the higher of the two, and here the readings differ`
    OTHERWISE `regulation 2 — the deduction, the ceiling being read as` c `and the regulation against section 47(b) as` ag `, for` i `and` g `, at` a

-- First level: the ceiling (fork F12).
@ref the Regulations of 5740-1980; fork F12
GIVEN rs IS A `The readings of the Regulations of 5740-1980`
      i  IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      g  IS AN `An individual's age and kind of payment, for the Regulations of 5740-1980`
      a  IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction under the Regulations of 5740-1980, reading them as` rs `, for` i `and` g `, at` a MEANS
    CONSIDER rs's `ceiling`
    WHEN `declined where the readings differ` THEN
        IF   `regulation 2 — resolving the regulation against section 47(b) as` (rs's `against section 47(b)`) `, the ceiling being` `the first rate of the paragraph` `, for` i `and` g `, at` a
             EQUALS `regulation 2 — resolving the regulation against section 47(b) as` (rs's `against section 47(b)`) `, the ceiling being` `every rate of the paragraph` `, for` i `and` g `, at` a
        THEN `regulation 2 — resolving the regulation against section 47(b) as` (rs's `against section 47(b)`) `, the ceiling being` `the first rate of the paragraph` `, for` i `and` g `, at` a
        ELSE `regulation 1 defines the ceiling of the deduction by the rates fixed in section 47(b)(1) or (2) and does not say whether that is the first rate or every rate of the paragraph, and here the readings differ`
    OTHERWISE `regulation 2 — resolving the regulation against section 47(b) as` (rs's `against section 47(b)`) `, the ceiling being` (rs's `ceiling`) `, for` i `and` g `, at` a

§§ `The deduction under s 47 with the Regulations, and the order with the s 45A credit`

-- Age 50 at the start of the tax year and not a beneficiary member: the Regulations' deduction takes the place of s 47(b)'s; otherwise IL-08's.
@ref ITO s 47(b), (b1), (d); the Regulations of 5740-1980
GIVEN rs IS A `The readings of the Regulations of 5740-1980`
      i  IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      g  IS AN `An individual's age and kind of payment, for the Regulations of 5740-1980`
      a  IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47 with the Regulations — the deduction taking the payment first, reading the Regulations as` rs `, for` i `and` g `, at` a MEANS
    IF   `one born on` (g's `date of birth`) `has completed 50 years at the start of tax year` (i's `tax year`)
         AND NOT `s 47(a)(7) — a beneficiary member:` i `, at` a
    THEN `the deduction under the Regulations of 5740-1980, reading them as` rs `, for` i `and` g `, at` a
    ELSE `s 47 — the deduction, the deduction taking the payment first, for` i `, at` a

@ref ITO s 47(b), (b1), (c), (d); s 45A; the Regulations of 5740-1980; fork F35
GIVEN rs IS A `The readings of the Regulations of 5740-1980`
      i  IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      g  IS AN `An individual's age and kind of payment, for the Regulations of 5740-1980`
      a  IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47 with the Regulations — the deduction, the section 45A credit taking the payment first, reading the Regulations as` rs `, for` i `and` g `, at` a MEANS
    IF   `first` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE min `first`
             (max 0 (`s 47 — the sums the deduction can take, for` i `, at` a
                     MINUS `s 47 and s 45A — the pension sums section 45A credits with nothing deducted, for` i `, at` a))
    WHERE `first` MEANS `s 47 with the Regulations — the deduction taking the payment first, reading the Regulations as` rs `, for` i `and` g `, at` a

@ref ITO s 47(b)-(d), lines 1778-1789; the Regulations of 5740-1980; fork F35
GIVEN rs IS A `The readings of the Regulations of 5740-1980`
      ro IS A `A reading of the order between the deduction under section 47 and the credit under section 45A`
      i  IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
      g  IS AN `An individual's age and kind of payment, for the Regulations of 5740-1980`
      a  IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction under section 47, reading the Regulations of 5740-1980 as` rs `and the order with the section 45A credit as` ro `, for` i `and` g `, at` a MEANS
    `for tax year` (i's `tax year`) `, row IL-27 answers`
        (CONSIDER ro
         WHEN `the deduction first` THEN `deduction first`
         WHEN `the credit first`    THEN `credit first`
         WHEN `the order the taxpayer chooses` `deduction first chosen`
             THEN IF `deduction first chosen` THEN `deduction first` ELSE `credit first`
         WHEN `declined where the order changes the answer`
             THEN IF   `deduction first` EQUALS `credit first`
                  THEN `deduction first`
                  ELSE `sections 47 and 45A do not say whether the deduction or the credit takes a payment first, and here the order changes the answer`)
    WHERE
        `deduction first` MEANS `s 47 with the Regulations — the deduction taking the payment first, reading the Regulations as` rs `, for` i `and` g `, at` a
        `credit first`    MEANS `s 47 with the Regulations — the deduction, the section 45A credit taking the payment first, reading the Regulations as` rs `, for` i `and` g `, at` a

@export The deduction from income, in NIS for a tax year from 2024, under Income Tax Ordinance s 47(b) and (b1) with the Regulations of 5740-1980 made under s 47(d): for an individual who has completed 50 years at the start of the tax year and is not a beneficiary member, 10.5% of the qualifying income to which s 47(b)(1) applies (more for one who paid for a pension only) and 7.5% of that to which s 47(b)(2) applies, to the ceiling of regulation 1; declines where the ceiling, the relation to s 47(b) or the order with the s 45A credit changes the answer
@ref ITO s 47(b)-(d), lines 1778-1789; the Regulations of 5740-1980, lines 14-25
GIVEN i IS AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
          @desc as for row IL-08's section 47
      g IS AN `An individual's age and kind of payment, for the Regulations of 5740-1980`
          @desc the date of birth and whether the sums were paid for a pension only
      a IS A `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year`
          @desc NIS; as for row IL-08's section 47
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` i `and` g `, at` a MEANS
    `the deduction under section 47, reading the Regulations of 5740-1980 as` `the Regulations of 5740-1980 — the readings row IL-27 takes` `and the order with the section 45A credit as` `section 47 — the reading this row takes of the order between the deduction and the section 45A credit` `, for` i `and` g `, at` a
